osphere with crew. But difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric, not willing to further education. Concerns: communication, adaptability.\n\nCandidate D: responds adequately to unexpected events, concentrates, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously. But hot temper, know-it-all, loner, arrogant, weak leadership. Concerns: communication, teamwork, stress? Not sure.\n\nWe need to choose best overall fit. Let's weigh criteria: reliability, stress resilience, technical competence, decision quality, attention, crew cooperation, communication, responsibility, adaptability.\n\nReliability: C (100% reliable), B (very conscientious), A (leadership but not sure reliability), D (takes responsibility seriously). So C and B top.\n\nStress resilience: B handles stress well, C keeps calm in crisis, D responds adequately to unexpected events (maybe okay), A unknown.\n\nTechnical competence: A sees complex connections, spatial vision, leadership; B good at weather, computer; C understands complicated technology, makes quick decisions; D solves problems extremely well.\n\nDecision quality: C makes correct decisions quickly, A anticipates dangerous situations, B good at assessing weather, D responds adequately.\n\nAttention: D concentrates well, B weak memory for numbers, A unknown, C unknown.\n\nCrew cooperation: C creates positive atmosphere, B uncooperative, D loner, A maybe show-off.\n\nCommunication: B pretentious, nasty remarks, wrong tone; C difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric; D know-it-all, hot temper, loner; A not open to new ideas, maybe poor communication.\n\nResponsibility: D takes responsibility seriously, A leadership, B conscientious, C reliable.\n\nAdaptability: B unknown, C not willing to further education, A not open to new ideas, D arrogant.\n\nOverall, C seems strong on reliability, crew atmosphere, decision quality, calmness, technical. Communication issues but maybe manageable. B strong on stress, technical, but communication and memory issues. D has responsibility but poor teamwork. A leadership but many concerns.\n\nThus likely C is best overall despite communication issues. So I will align with Sarah's recommendation for C, but need to provide reasoning and maybe ask about B's memory for numbers or A's stress. But we need to make a contribution: maybe I will support Candidate C, but note need to verify B's memory impact. Or I could shift to C.\n\nGiven the current leading candidate is C per Sarah, I can say I now also recommend C, because reliability and crew atmosphere outweigh B's memory and communication concerns. Provide evidence: C 100% reliable, positive crew atmosphere, quick correct decisions; B's weak memory for numbers could affect attention.\n\nThus my vote: Candidate C.\n\nLet's craft PUBLIC_MESSAGE: \"I agree with Sarah that Candidate C is the strongest overall. While B is conscientious and stress\u2011resilient, his weak memory for numbers and uncooperative demeanor raise safety concerns. Candidate C\u2019s 100\u202f% reliability, ability to keep calm in crisis, and proven positive crew atmosphere directly address the core criteria. Therefore I now recommend Candidate C.\"\n\nMake sure to reference discussion: mention Emily's vote for B, Sarah's vote for C, and James's own earlier info about D.\n\nOk."}
